  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nBeyond this afternoon's few showers and storms over the Coastal \nPlains from the trough riding the southwestern periphery of the \nridge ushering moisture, mid-level ridging will flatten out over the \nsouthern CONUS and lead to near normal moisture, hot, and generally \nrain-free conditions into the middle of next week. Heat indices will \npeak around 110 over the Coastal Plains daily, with max temperatures \nranging from 90-105 degrees and low temperatures in the mid to upper \n70s. Therefore, a moderate to major risk of heat-related impacts \nwill remain South Texas' greatest weather concern.\n\nHeading into the latter part of next week, a mid to upper level \ntrough is expected to push eastward across the Midwest to Great \nLakes region, potentially reflecting all the way south into parts of \nTexas. Currently, any impacts or increased rain chances remain \nnorth of our area.",
